fujinet-go-h89-desktop -- milestone log
======================================

The plan is the family's (see fujinet-go-adam-desktop/PORTING.md): one C API
in core/, four native frontends, FujiNet in-process, one shared settings
store, a native debugger everywhere, no panels visible at startup,
clone-and-build CI. The core is VirtualH89 (mgarlanger, BSD-3), vendored
and adapted in core/v89 with this app's own layer in core/machine.
Nothing below is marked done on "it compiles".

M0  scaffold                                                          [x]
  [x] root CMakeLists (VERSION 0.1.0, FRONTEND switch, WITH_H89_ROMS OFF,
      no_embedded_roms + check_exports registration, icon loop, CPack
      DEB/RPM/TGZ), .gitignore, LICENSE, mingw toolchain
  [x] cmake/Dependencies.cmake pins fujinet-firmware master b13c4ad7a (the
      plan named c68e863, a side-branch commit; master has everything it
      had -- FujiBus on RS232, TCP_NODELAY on BoIP -- and the sms build
      script's patches apply to it unchanged)
  [x] tools/fujinet: PC target RS232, BoIP 11512, web UI 11513
  [x] icons: the family mark on the Heathkit nameplate -- black plate, gold
      frame, cream stones, a cream rim on the black centre stone
  verify: libfujinet built from master in one go; check_exports passes
      (fujinet_desktop_* and fujinet_android_submit_sam_audio only)

M1  emulator core, headless                                           [x]
  [x] core/v89: VirtualH89 d1dea92 minus the GUIs, main, consoles, Z47,
      disassembler, property reader, ROM and font arrays
  [x] MachineContext: the wall clock and GPP listeners per machine
  [x] Z80::runCycles + instruction/IO/memory hooks + IM 2; no SIGALRM
  [x] Machine (the builder, from h89_config), IntrController (H37 + MMS
      77316 together), H89Timer slices, H19Terminal, H19Render (444-29)
  [x] Host: thread, 2 ms slices in 16 ms batches on a deadline ladder,
      frame slot, run lock, key ring, warp (real time while FujiNet talks)
  [x] romset: the ROM table by CRC; MAME's zips read with puff
  [x] config: model, memory, P503, monitor, speed-up, SW401/402/501 (per
      monitor, auto from the slots), P504-506 cards, every drive type,
      MMS 77320, CP/NET; validation; key/value access
  [x] h89_headless (scripted: --until/--type/--key/--disk/--screen/--ppm)
  [x] Windows: compat_posix.h (fnmatch, ffs, bzero, mkdir, localtime_r,
      O_BINARY)
  verify: ctest 10/10 on Linux, and the same tests pass under Wine from the
      mingw cross-build; MTR-90 reaches "H:" in 3 s; boot_smoke measures
      500.0 slices/s

M2  FujiNet card + H17 images                                         [x]
  [x] FujiNetCard: 82C55 mode 2 at 0xD0-D3, portio.c's handshake, EN
      reset/download mode, rawpipe (POSIX/Winsock, lazy reconnect)
  [x] H17Image: raw (both side orders), H8D (HDOS volume from the label),
      H17Disk v2 and the draft (captured sectors); write-back; blank images
  [x] the sector layout measured from the captured HDOS disks (header sync
      at 10, data sync at 32)
  [x] drive API (h89drives.h), debounced write-back from the host thread
  verify: HDOS 2.0 boots from its distribution disk to its date prompt
      (hdos_boot test; it detects the console baud rate from a SPACE);
      card test against a loopback peer, also under Wine
  [x] session layer (core/src): settings, paths, the FujiNet runtime
      loader (listen first, then the machine dials), ROM import, media
      routing, drives, audio; h89_session_run drives it headless
  [x] fujibus_smoke: one FujiBus exchange through the card against the real
      libfujinet, no ROMs (runs in CI wherever the runtime is built)
  [x] h89_headless --prompt: wait for a prompt at the cursor (HDOS drops
      what is typed ahead of one)
  verify: tools/e2e/hdos-fujidev.sh -- HDOS 2.0 runs fujinet-lib's FUJIDEV
      from SY1: against the in-process FujiNet: 23 of 24 pass; the one
      failure is the firmware's (an empty filename does not clear a device
      slot -- fujiDevice.cpp only invalidates its host slot), not the pipe;
      fujibus_smoke: 140-byte adapter config, checksum good

M3  disks                                                             [x]
  [x] SoftDisk: IMD / TD0 (read-only) / VirtualH89 sector + raw images in
      one in-memory model, written back as themselves (an untouched IMD
      byte for byte); replaces VirtualH89's three image classes
  [x] WD1797 Write Track (index to index, Lost Data), TrackFormatter (FM
      and MFM codes); per-track density; Read Address with real IDs;
      Write Sector/Track refused at once on a protected disk
  [x] runtime mount on the H37 and MMS 77316 (Drives.cpp), media probe
      telling raw floppy from H17 raw images
  [x] MMS 77320: unit files in data/sasi; VirtualH89's write path fixed
      (status byte after a write, multi-block REQ, Write Long, sense as
      data-in, a clean status per command)
  [x] CP/NET HostFileBdos: HOME fallback on Windows, Select Disk's
      uninitialised stat fixed
  verify: soft_disk, sasi, hostfile_bdos tests (Linux and under Wine);
      HDOS INIT on a blank .h8d, PIP a file to it, a fresh boot TYPEs it
  [x] CP/M (SEBHC's distributions, tools/disks/fetch-disks.sh): 2.2.04 boots
      from the H17 and CONFIGURs itself; MOVCPM17 64 * + SYSGEN write a 64K
      system to the boot tracks; 2.2.04 with BIOS-80 boots from ImageDisk on
      the Z-89-37
  [x] fixed on the way: the session left 444-19 unmapped without an H-88-1
      (MTR-90 boots the Z-89-37 through its routines: the boot slid through
      zeros); it is CPU-board equipment, mapped whenever imported and needed
      for any floppy controller. The WD1797's idle status kept Index in bit
      1 after Type II/III commands, where it is DRQ: FORMAT read it as an
      error after the first track
  [x] h89_session_run --debug CMD: a debugger command mid-script
  verify: tools/e2e/cpm-h37-format.sh (FORMAT an empty IMD on the Z-89-37,
      PIP to it, a fresh session STATs it), tools/e2e/cpm-fujidev.sh (64K
      CP/M on the H17 runs FUJIDEV: 23/24, the firmware's known failure);
      soft_disk checks the idle status bits after Type I and Type III.
      The MMS 77316 has no public CP/M boot disk: only its tests cover it
